{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"ALSA-2026:95100","published":"2026-11-04T00:00:00Z","modified":"2026-11-04T22:15:02.260844526Z","related":["CVE-2026-52929","CVE-2026-64541","CVE-2026-74586","CVE-2026-80863","CVE-2026-80864","CVE-2026-89488"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-52929","CVE-2026-64541","CVE-2026-74586","CVE-2026-80863","CVE-2026-80864","CVE-2026-89488"],"summary":"Important: kernel-rt security, bug fix, and enhancement update","details":"The kernel-rt packages provide the Real Time Linux Kernel, which enables fine-tuning for systems with extremely high determinism requirements.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * kernel: sctp: stream: fully roll back denied add-stream state (CVE-2026-52929)\n  * kernel: net/smc: fix UAF in smc_cdc_rx_handler() by pinning the socket (CVE-2026-64541)\n  * kernel: sctp: clear new_transport when removing a peer (CVE-2026-74586)\n  * kernel: RDMA/rxe: Fix responder UAF on IB_QP_MAX_DEST_RD_ATOMIC modify_qp (CVE-2026-80864)\n  * kernel: RDMA/rxe: Fix OOB in free_rd_atomic_resources() (CVE-2026-80863)\n  * kernel: openvswitch: Fix CT limit teardown use-after-free (CVE-2026-89488)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * AlmaLinux8.10 - s390/smp: Remove conditional emergency signal usage (JIRA:RHEL-298849)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"kernel-rt","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/kernel-rt"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.18.0-553.184.1.rt7.525.el8_10"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/AlmaLinux/osv-database/blob/master/advisories/almalinux8/ALSA-2026:95100.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-rt-core","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/kernel-rt-core"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.18.0-553.184.1.rt7.525.el8_10